<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Okehazama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1560</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Okehazama was fought in June 1560 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owari-province">Owari Province</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> with a small force made a surprise attack on the much larger army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imagawa-yoshimoto">Imagawa Yoshimoto</a>, which was resting during its march west. Yoshimoto was killed and the Imagawa never recovered. The victory made Nobunaga's reputation and allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> to break away from the Imagawa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-okehazama.jpg" alt="Battle of Okehazama" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utagawa Toyonobu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bish%C5%AB_Okehazama-gassen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
